      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Given the system of equations below, what is the value of $p - q$?\n\n$\\{2p=14; p+4q=39$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "We will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. \n\nUsing the first equation, we can isolate $p$ by dividing both sides by $2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2p & =14 \\\\ p & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $p=7$ into the second equation and solve for $q:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p+4q & =39 \\\\ (7)+4q & =39 \\\\ 4q & =32 \\\\ q & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $p-q=7-(8)=-1.$",
