      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Given the system of equations below, what is the value of $a - b$?\n\n$\\{-3a-3b=45; -3a+b=-3$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "We will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. \n\nUsing the second equation, we can isolate $b$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3a+b & =-3 \\\\ b & =-3+3a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $b=-3+3a$ into the first equation and solve for $a:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3a-3b & =45 \\\\ -3a-3(-3+3a) & =45 \\\\ -3a+9-9a & =45 \\\\ -12a+9 & =45 \\\\ -12a & =36 \\\\ a & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $a=-3$ into $b=-3+3a,$ we can then find the value of $b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & =-3+3(-3) \\\\ b & =-12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a-b=-3-(-12)=9.$",
